 "structural_change": "PL-GUNIT (PARENTS-LANDED 10-18, landed-regions-standard-1018): dsdv_gunit as a LANDED parent from tools/landed_parent/lp.py (reschedule mode): two clock regions, hc = L0/L0r/L4/L4r/L5/L5f (HC subsystem above the stop) and rt = L2/L1/L1f x4/L1c/L3 (stop + router), each its own clock port and local tree; the ONLY crossing is the stop boundary L0|L2: 13 landings (1,655 b, 8,444 flops, +3 edges each), 1-bit reset runs depth 4. Every stacked leaf pair talks both ways, so any split is a cross-region loop: no offset schedule keeps the flat calendar; the compiler takes the re-schedule (N-side rung +3 each way, HC +6, router 0; results/arch/landed_parent_1018/gunit/dsdv_gunit_lp_record.json). Floorplan (43.2 lattice, 950.4 x 1468.8): col A stack L3/L1/L2 | 86.4 landing channel | L0/L4/L5; col B fronts f0..f2 beside L3/L1/L2 and L0r/L4r/L5f beside L0/L4/L5; col C f3 + L1c (collector E of the fronts). DIAGNOSTIC: L5 and L1f are stand-ins from their --cts gate odbs (no closed view: L5 regate died in synth, L1f pin-flop spread 114 TT). | GUNIT3 10-20: re-kit for L5 n32 (388.8 wide) and L1f 302.4x345.6 (2x2 fronts, L1c hub under the B|C gap, hc L0r/L4r/L5f at x 475.2); outline 1123.2 x 1468.8",
